1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:04,184
Every morning, planes drew white lines
across the sky over Addis.

2
00:00:03,984 --> 00:00:06,390
I used to think they were writing to me.

3
00:00:07,400 --> 00:00:08,602
So I chased them.

4
00:00:08,402 --> 00:00:12,139
Documentaries at midnight, not to study,
just to be near it.

5
00:00:11,939 --> 00:00:14,320
Whatever I could find online, I read.

6
00:00:15,400 --> 00:00:18,490
I watched landings the way other kids
watched football.

7
00:00:20,400 --> 00:00:24,214
Then Ethiopian Airlines opened a
sponsored trainee pilot program.

8
00:00:24,014 --> 00:00:24,770
I applied.

9
00:00:26,400 --> 00:00:31,420
Age. Documents. Written test. Passed.
Interview. Passed.

10
00:00:32,400 --> 00:00:37,174
In the simulator, my hands knew what to
do before I did. English proficiency.

11
00:00:36,974 --> 00:00:37,590
Passed.

12
00:00:39,400 --> 00:00:42,670
One test left. The medical. My eyes.

13
00:00:44,400 --> 00:00:47,740
Not cleared. Two words, and the sky
closed.

14
00:00:50,400 --> 00:00:52,040
For weeks, I couldn't look up.

15
00:00:55,400 --> 00:00:59,386
But the sky never asked for my eyes. It
asked for my curiosity.

16
00:00:59,186 --> 00:01:01,610
So I kept learning, and I built this.

17
00:01:04,400 --> 00:01:08,036
My eyes failed one test. My curiosity
hasn't failed one yet.

18
00:01:07,836 --> 00:01:09,410
I'm not done looking up.
